<title>PAKISTAN: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>PAKISTAN GOVERNMENT LIST (961105)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  *  5 Nov 96 - President Farooq Leghari sacked prime	 *</p>
<p>  *		 minister Benazir Bhutto, dissolved	    *</p>
<p>  *		 parliament and called general elections     *</p>
<p>  *		 for February 3 1997. Meraj Khalid was named *</p>
<p>  *		 caretaker prime minister and a nine-member  *</p>
<p>  *		 cabinet was sworn in.			     *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p> President......................................Farooq LEGHARI</p>
<p>(Elected 13 Nov 93 for a five-year term)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Caretaker Prime Minister (Apptd 5 Nov 96)........Meraj KHALID</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (portfolios not known)</p>
<p>Sahibzada Yaqub KHAN</p>
<p>Shahid HAMID</p>
<p>Shafqat MAHMOOD</p>
<p>Javaid JABBAR</p>
<p>Irshad Ahmed HAQQANI</p>
<p>Omar AFRIDI</p>
<p>Sadiq Nawaz AWAN</p>
<p>Syeda Abida HUSSAIN</p>
<p>Muhammad ZUBAIR</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central bank Governor..........................Mohammad YAQUB</p>
<p>(State Bank of Pakistan)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			     (End Government List)</p>
